  },
  "content": [
    {
      "type": "para",
      "id": "para-00001",
      "segmentId": "m00316:para:para-00001"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "id": "para-00002",
      "segmentId": "m00316:para:para-00002"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "id": "para-00003",
      "segmentId": "m00316:para:para-00003"
    },
    {
      "type": "figure",
      "id": "fig-00001",
      "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
      "caption": null,
      "media": {
        "alt": {
          "segmentId": "m00316:alt:fig-00001-alt",
          "text": "The first step of D N A synthesis. A deoxynucleoside and silica support are reacted to form a product where -O-Ph is replaced by the silica support."
        },
        "src": "../../media/OChem_28_07_001.jpg",
        "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "figure",
      "id": "fig-00002",
      "class": "unnumbered",
      "caption": null,
      "media": {
        "alt": {
          "segmentId": "m00316:alt:fig-00002-alt",
          "text": "The figure shows the structure of four bases named N-protected adenine, N-protected guanine, N-protected cytosine, and thymine. Wavy line denotes bond extension."
        },
        "src": "../../media/OChem_28_07_002.jpg",
        "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "id": "para-00004",
      "segmentId": "m00316:para:para-00004"
    },
    {
      "type": "figure",
      "id": "fig-00003",
      "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
      "caption": null,
      "media": {
        "alt": {
          "segmentId": "m00316:alt:fig-00003-alt",
          "text": "The reaction of nucleoside with dichloroacetic acid in dichloromethane removes the D M T protecting group from the hydroxyl of the nucleoside attached to the silica surface in the product."
        },
        "src": "../../media/OChem_28_07_003.jpg",
        "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "id": "para-00005",
      "segmentId": "m00316:para:para-00005"
    },
    {
      "type": "figure",
      "id": "fig-00004",
      "class": "unnumbered",
      "caption": null,
      "media": {
        "alt": {
          "segmentId": "m00316:alt:fig-00004-alt",
          "text": "The third step of D N A synthesis. The reaction of two nucleosides in presence of tetrazole forms a product where the phosphoramidite group is replaced by the phosphite group."
        },
        "src": "../../media/OChem_28_07_004.jpg",
        "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "id": "para-00006",
      "segmentId": "m00316:para:para-00006"
    },
    {
      "type": "figure",
      "id": "fig-00005",
      "class": "unnumbered",
      "caption": null,
      "media": {
        "alt": {
          "segmentId": "m00316:alt:fig-00005-alt",
          "text": "The fourth step of D N A synthesis. It involves the oxidation of the phosphite product to phosphate by reaction with iodine along with 2,6 dimethylpyridine in aqueous tetrahydrofuran."
        },
        "src": "../../media/OChem_28_07_005.jpg",
        "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "id": "para-00007",
      "segmentId": "m00316:para:para-00007"
    },
    {
      "type": "figure",
      "id": "fig-00006",
      "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
      "caption": null,
      "media": {
        "alt": {
          "segmentId": "m00316:alt:fig-00006-alt",
          "text": "The last step of D N A synthesis. Two deoxynucleosides of a polynucleotide chain react with aqueous ammonia. The product has no protected groups."
        },
        "src": "../../media/OChem_28_07_006.jpg",
        "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
      }
    },
